course: dictionary
lesson: 37
title: The many meanings of accent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Holly's family moved from England to Australia, and her accent sounded different.» Here accent means the way people from a place say words.
explain: Accent can also mean the extra force you put on one part of a word. This is called stress. Say PRE-sent (a gift) and pre-SENT (to show). The capital letters show the stressed part, and stress can change what the word means.
explain: Never use an accent to make fun of someone. Everyone has one, and an accent shows where a person grew up. «Learning another language is hard, and many people speak two or more, so never copy or tease an accent.»
fact: An accent is the way people from a place pronounce a language.
fact: An accent can also be the stress, the extra force on one part of a word.
fact: A small mark above or below a letter can be an accent too, as in café.
fact: «Accents grow from the people who settle a place», so the Australian accent grew from settlers from London, south-east England and Ireland.
fact: In music, an accent is a note played louder than the notes around it.
exercise: «Holly's family moved from England to Australia, and kids copied her accent.» In this sentence, what does accent mean? | A small mark above a letter | A tall building on a hill | *The way people from a place pronounce words | A louder note in a song
exercise: In PRE-sent (a gift) and pre-SENT (to show), the capital letters show where the accent falls. What is the accent in these words? | A rule for spelling | A word from another country | *The extra force on one part of the word | A small mark over the letter e
exercise: «Learning another language is hard, so never copy or tease an accent.» What should you do with someone's accent? | Copy it loudly so people laugh | Ask them to hide it | Tease them until they change it | *Respect it, because everyone has one
test: The sentence «Accents grow from the people who settle a place» tells you where accents come from. Where do they come from? | A small mark above a letter | A dictionary | *The people who settled the place and their mix of voices | Only from music lessons
test: In music, what is an accent? | *A note played louder than the others | A word from another language | A quiet pause between two songs | A small mark above a letter
exam: In «Put the accent on the second part of the word», what does accent mean? | A small mark above a letter | *The stress, or extra force, on one part of the word | The way people from a place talk | A quiet note in music
